  "worked_solution": "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (20t-12{t}^{2})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =10{t}^{2}-4{t}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(1)=8.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8 & =10(1)^{2}-4(1)^{3}+C \\\\ 8 & =6+C \\\\ C & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=10{t}^{2}-4{t}^{3}+2.$\n\nWe evaluate the velocity at time $t=2\\,\\text{s}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =10(2)^{2}-4(2)^{3}+2 \\\\  & =40-32+2 \\\\  & =10\\,\\text{ft}/\\text{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the speed is equal to $|v(t)|$, we conclude that the speed of the particle is $10\\,\\text{ft}/\\text{s}.$",
